{"id":"u-e089ae81-9c23-44fa-8bc4-a7f1c483994d","src":"community","title":"Train like Bane: Get Jacked at Home","author":"Wyatt D.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/train-like-bane-get-jacked-at-home-10","desc":"The purpose of this program is simple - build hypertrophy within the confines of your own home.\n\nThis Program will focus on a simple progression of Push-Ups, Rows, and Squats. These are some of the best all around movements to use if you're starting out, as they build a base for strength in the future and they bolster you're ability to move in your day-to-day life.\n\nEach week you will add an extra 2 sets to your workout. It is meant to start off light and build up.\n\nIf it is too challenging at first, do less repititions per excersise. If it is not challenging enough, you can add weight by using everyday household items (i.e. two gallons of liquid, a stack of books, a chair, e.t.c.). \n\nThe purpose of adding 2 sets every week is to make increase hypertrophy from week to week. Ideally, from week to week the same number of sets should be less challenging. Challenging is what we're looking for here, as this is the greatest way to stimulate muscle growth (in bro-science terms.)\n\nThe final week is a deload week to eleviate some fatigue to prepare you for your next cycle. All of your training will be cut in half from the previous week, and you will see the improvements you've made since you started.\n\nWith each passing week each movement will get a bit easier, but you will make it that much harder. This is the name of the game in the weightlifting world, and anything you do in life really: progressive overload.\n\nAlong with the core movements I have added additional accessory movements to provide more overrall growth, but it also provides you with something yo change it up with.\n\nFeel free to add variations and modifications as you please. Now get after it.\n\n\nThumbnail credit: fandom.com","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Bodyweight Fitness","Athletics"],"equipment":["At Home"],"minutes":30,"joins":354,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-21T11:34:24.872Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push Day","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Push Up (Knees)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Pike Push Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Dips Between Chairs","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Push Up (Incline)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Row Between Chairs","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Iron Cross","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}],"note":"10-15 on each side"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Side Plank","sets":[{"sec":60,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Dead Hang","sets":[{"sec":30,"rpe":8,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Row Between Chairs","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Iron Cross","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Squat (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lunge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"10-20 Each side"}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Lunge","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}],"note":"10-20 Each side"},{"n":"Jump Squat","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Squat (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lunge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}],"note":"10-20 Each Side"}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Push Up (Knees)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Pike Push Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]},{"n":"Dips Between Chairs","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":8.5,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Push Up","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Push Up (Incline)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":9,"x":2}]}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Row Between Chairs","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":